        "\n",
        "# Numerical Methods\n",
        "\n",
        "## Discretizing functions\n",
        "\n",
        "- simplest: finite number of $x_i$ and $y_i = f(x_i)$ (with $i = 1, \\dots , N$)\n",
        "- Points $x_i$ can be regularly spaced\n",
        "- Accuracy depends on:\n",
        "  - how smooth the real function is\n",
        "  - how close the points are taken\n",
        "But more points $\\longrightarrow$ **more data**, **slower**\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Discretizing functions\n"
      ],
      "id": "d873386e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "from numpy import pi, sin, cos, sqrt, linspace\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "for j, n in enumerate(list([1000])):\n",
        "  x = linspace(0, 12*pi, n)\n",
        "  y = 0.2 * x * sin(x)\n",
        "  plt.plot(x, y)\n",
        "  ax = plt.gca()\n",
        "  ax.set_aspect(\"equal\")\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"x\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"y\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "186f0ce1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
