      "source": [
        "- How many points should be taken?\n",
        "- More points take up more memory and require more calculations\n",
        "- Choose interval length and stepsize according to function/problem\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Solving Equations: Root Finding \n",
        "\n",
        "Example: polynomial equations in one variable:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\begin{aligned}\n",
        "  \\textrm{Equation} \\qquad&\\qquad \\textrm{(partial) solution}\\\\\n",
        "  4 x - 3 = 5 \\qquad&\\qquad x = 2\\\\\n",
        "  2 x^2 - x + 2 = 0 \\qquad&\\qquad x_\\pm = \\frac{1 \\pm i\\sqrt{15}}{4}\\\\\n",
        "  x^3 - 27 = 0 \\qquad&\\qquad (x - 3) (x^2 + 3x + 9)\\\\\n",
        "  x^5 - x^3 = 0 \\qquad&\\qquad x^3 (x^2 - 1)\\\\\n",
        "  x^3 - x^2 + x - 1 = 0 \\qquad&\\qquad \\\\\n",
        "\\end{aligned}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Solving Transcendental Equations\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\begin{aligned}\n",
        "  \\textrm{Equation} \\qquad&\\qquad \\textrm{(partial) solution}\\\\\n",
        "  e^x = 3 \\qquad&\\qquad x = \\ln 3\\\\\n",
        "  2^x = 3x - 2 \\qquad&\\qquad x = 2\\quad\\textrm{by sketch}\\\\\n",
        "  2^x = 3x - 1 \\qquad&\\qquad x = 1, 3\\\\\n",
        "  \\tanh(x) = 1/x^2 \\qquad&\\qquad x \\approx , \\textrm{(numerical) real-valued} \\\\\n",
        "  \\sin(x) = x \\qquad&\\qquad x = 0, \\textrm{but complex solutions} \\\\\n",
        "\\end{aligned}\n",
        "$$\n"
      ],
      "id": "83559fde"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
